    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` and wrote 59 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. The rules are split into small helpers: validation, per-line net and tax, and the credit split. Each function's cyclomatic complexity is well under 10, so the CRAP gate depends only on how many lines the tests execute, which the tests should cover thoroughly. Rounding is `ROUND_HALF_UP` per line, and every money output is quantized to two decimal places. The tests cover the rules in `spec.md`, including the bulk-discount boundary at 9 and 10 units, the multiplicative stacking of discounts, per-line rounding, and every `ValueError` case. I could not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates myself, since only the pytest command was allowed, so those are unverified. One judgment call: a credit with more than two decimal places is rounded in the output, because the spec requires two decimal places everywhere.",
